Add a Tab Control
If you are going to create a tabbed dialog, you first have to create the Tab Control. The tab control
resembles a notebook that contains any number of pages (tabs). The user can navigate between different
tabs and/or sections of information within the dialog box.
Note
Do not confuse the tab control with the tabs themselves. The tab control is the container that holds the
individual tabs (pages).
When the user selects another tab, the Dialog calls the Callback Method, which in turn executes the
actions you programmed with the first parameter you typed in as Callback Argument.
To add it to your dialog:
• Right-click the tab Elements and select New Tab Control.
• Type in the Name of the tab control. A Method object can call this dialog item using the Name you
typed in.
• Type in the Callback Argument, which will be passed to the callback method.
• Type in the X-coordinate and the Y-coordinate of the tab control in the Dialog.
The position corresponds to the average width of characters of your system font, not to pixels. Changing
the font size under Personalization > Font affects this setting.
• Type in the Width and the Height of the tab control in the Dialog. The default value of 0 sets the height
and the width to the values defined by us.
• To insert the Tab Control into your dialog, click OK.
Add a Tab Control
Plant Simulation Help 10-1431
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• To add one Tab at the time to the Tab Control, click it with the right mouse button on the tab Elements
and select New Tab Page on the context menu.
• To change the order of the tabs in the dialog, select a tab 
  on the tab Elements, hold down Shift and
press the Up arrow to move this tab to the left or press the Down arrow to move this tab to the right.
The dialog shows the first tab in the structure as the leftmost tab.
Go to Program Actions which the Dialog Items Execute
Compare New Tab Control in the Object Reference
Back to Design a Tabbed Dialog
Add Tabs to a Tab Control
You can add individual tabs to the Tab Control, which is the container for the tabs.
To add one Tab at a time to the Tab Control:
• Right-click the tab Elements and select New Tab Page.
• Enter the Name of the tab into the dialog Dialog Item Tab Page. A Method object can call this dialog
item using the Name you entered.
• Enter the Caption of the tab. A caption is especially handy if you develop libraries in several languages
and want the user to be able to switch languages. In addition you can enter special characters and
blanks. The tab on the tab control shows this caption as the title on the tab itself.
• To insert the dialog item into your dialog, click OK.
Add Tabs to a Tab Control
10-1432 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• To change the order of the tabs in the dialog, select a tab on the tab Elements, hold down Shift and
press the Up arrow to move this tab to the left or the Down arrow to move it to the right. The dialog
shows the first tab in the structure as the leftmost tab.
