Add a List Box
A List Box displays a list of choices. The user can double-click one of the items in the list to select it. As
opposed to the drop-down list box, the list box has a fixed size and does not collapse.
To add it to your dialog:
• Right-click the tab Elements and select New List Box.
Add a List Box
Plant Simulation Help 10-1433
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• Type in the Name of the list box. A Method object can call this dialog item using the Name you typed in.
• Type in the Callback Argument, which will be passed to the callback method.
• Type the X-coordinate and the Y-coordinate of the list box in the Dialog.
The position corresponds to the average width of characters of your system font, not to pixels. Changing
the font size under Personalization > Font affects this setting.
Note
If you cannot see a dialog item after you inserted it, check the settings for the position first. If you
typed in identical values for different dialog items, the Dialog places them on top of each other, so
that you can only see the first item(s) you inserted.
• Type the Width and the Height of the list box in the Dialog. If you do not type in values, the Dialog
sets the width and height to the values defined by us. When you type in a value for the height, it adds a
vertical scrollbar to the list, if the list contains more items than the height can display.
• Click Items and type the items the list box displays in the dialog Items.
◦ To add an item to the list field, type its name into the text box and click Insert or press the Enter key.
◦ Repeat this for all the items you want to add.
◦ To delete an item from the list, select it in the list field and click Delete.
◦ To move an item up one position in the list, select it in the list field and click Move Up.
◦ To change the name of an item in the list, select it in the list field, type another name into the text
box, and click Rename.
◦ To apply the items you typed in and to close the dialog, click OK.
◦ To discard what you have done so far, click Cancel.
Add a List Box
10-1434 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• Select if you want to Enable the list box or not.
• To insert the dialog item into your dialog, click OK.
Go to Program Actions which the Dialog Items Execute
Compare New List Box in the Object Reference
